<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌊 LIVE WAVE HEIGHT/PERIOD/DIRECTION</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wave_combined/legend.png?v=glwu-20261010-0700Z-combined-r12-stream-f7-tx4" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Base color = wave height, exact bin colors (see table). Model height max this run: <b>5.4 ft</b>. Arrows point where the waves travel (WVDIR + 180&deg;). White halo numbers are the actual peak period at that spot (seconds between crests, e.g. 4.2s), drawn in the same style as the arrows and placed just above them; extra numbers mark spots where the period changes sharply even between arrows. Period max now <b>7.7s</b>, mean travel <b>134&deg; (SE)</b>. Significant height = average of highest third of waves.</p><p><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis), 6-hourly cycles</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP Great Lakes Wave Unstructured v2.1 (GLWUv2.1, WAVEWATCH III) — HTSGW height + PERPW peak period + WVDIR direction, surface analysis (single cycle)<br/><a href="https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/pub/data/nccf/com/glwu/prod/glwu.20261010/glwu.grlc_2p5km.t07z.grib2">https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/pub/data/nccf/com/glwu/prod/glwu.20261010/glwu.grlc_2p5km.t07z.grib2</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE WAVE HEIGHT/PERIOD/DIRECTION</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<p>Wave height color + actual peak-period numbers + travel arrows, all from one GLWU cycle.</p><p><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wave_combined/legend.png?v=glwu-20261010-0700Z-combined-r12-stream-f7-tx4" width="600" alt="key"></p><p>Base color = wave height, exact bin colors (see table). Model height max this run: <b>5.4 ft</b>. Arrows point where the waves travel (WVDIR + 180&deg;). White halo numbers are the actual peak period at that spot (seconds between crests, e.g. 4.2s), drawn in the same style as the arrows and placed just above them; extra numbers mark spots where the period changes sharply even between arrows. Period max now <b>7.7s</b>, mean travel <b>134&deg; (SE)</b>. Significant height = average of highest third of waves.</p>]]></description>
      <GroundOverlay>
        <name>🌊 LIVE WAVE HEIGHT/PERIOD/DIRECTION</name>
        <drawOrder>10</drawOrder>
        <Icon>
          <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wave_combined/current.png?v=glwu-20261010-0700Z-combined-r12-stream-f7-tx4</href>
          <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
          <refreshInterval>300</refreshInterval>
        </Icon>
        <LatLonBox>
          <north>49.5</north>
          <south>40.5</south>
          <east>-73.5</east>
          <west>-93.0</west>
        </LatLonBox>
      </GroundOverlay>
    </Folder>
  </Document>
